--  D1113, [1970]: `link(symbol: "main")` on the hosted entry names the
--  linkage the entry has without it, as a program moved from firmware,
--  where the prefix is how an entry gets that symbol, still spells it.
--  It stands beside the library's own C view of `main` as the entry, not
--  as a second declaration of the symbol.
link(symbol: "main") public main: () -> (code: i32) =
    code = 0
end main
